The attached image conceptually represents the "dendrimer-like" internal structure of the alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle (Nano-11), as described in the provided PDF. It shows a cross-section of a spherical particle with a dense, highly branched network radiating from a central core, illustrating the structural basis for its "high molecular density which increases from the center to the surface of the particle." This unique, dendrimer-like architecture, derived from phytoglycogen, is central to Nano-11's efficacy as a vaccine adjuvant due to its ability to efficiently adsorb antigens and be taken up by dendritic cells.